-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":{"goal":"Verify focus is kept in CSS and controls are real elements in JSX, then judge keyboard reachability","inputs":{"$cl_type":"t19"},"steps":[{"action":"read","args":{"path":{"$input":"cssPath"}},"check":"focus-css","save":"css"},{"action":"read","args":{"path":{"$input":"jsxPath"}},"check":"a11y-jsx","save":"jsx"},{"judge":"keyboard-path"}]},"key":"check-access","section":"procedures"}
P check-access(cssPath:str jsxPath:str):css=workspace.read(path:cssPath) C focus-css; jsx=workspace.read(path:jsxPath) C a11y-jsx; J keyboard-path -- Verify focus is kept in CSS and controls are real elements in JSX, then judge keyboard reachability
V P check-access -> script why:"typed manual runner; stops at every judgement"
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":{"constraints":"Tab through the rendered component in a browser tab. preview.taste lists unnamed controls and small targets; any unnamed control is fix.","options":["yes","fix"],"question":"Can every action be reached and used with the keyboard alone, with a visible focus ring?"},"key":"keyboard-path","section":"judge"}
J keyboard-path yes|fix:"Can every action be reached and used with the keyboard alone, with a visible focus ring?" -- Tab through the rendered component in a browser tab. preview.taste lists unnamed controls and small targets; any unnamed control is fix.
V J keyboard-path -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":{"failure":"outline: none without a replacement","recovery":"Delete it; the .nx focus ring already applies"},"key":"0","section":"pitfalls"}
X outline: none without a replacement -> Delete it; the .nx focus ring already applies
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":{"failure":"Tooltip text used as the only label","recovery":"Pass label to IconButton (aria-label + title)"},"key":"1","section":"pitfalls"}
X Tooltip text used as the only label -> Pass label to IconButton (aria-label + title)
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Focus-not-obscured (2.4.11) and drag alternatives (2.5.7) have no automatic check yet: they need a Tab walk and an Arrange journey in the taste lens.","key":"0","section":"frontier"}
F Focus-not-obscured (2.4.11) and drag alternatives (2.5.7) have no automatic check yet: they need a Tab walk and an Arrange journey in the taste lens.
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Focus is never removed: .nx :focus-visible draws var(--nx-focus) (2px background gap + accent ring). Custom controls keep it; inputs may use inset 0 0 0 1px var(--nx-accent-hi) on :focus.","key":"0","section":"guidance"}
M design "Focus is never removed: .nx :focus-visible draws var(--nx-focus) (2px background gap + accent ring). Custom controls keep it; inputs may use inset 0 0 0 1px var(--nx-accent-hi) on :focus." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Every icon-only control has a label (IconButton label=...); decorative icons are aria-hidden (Icon does it).","key":"1","section":"guidance"}
M design "Every icon-only control has a label (IconButton label=...); decorative icons are aria-hidden (Icon does it)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Real elements: <button type=button> for actions, <a> for navigation, <label> around inputs. Choice groups use role=radiogroup + aria-checked (Segmented); menus/lists use role=menuitem/option with useRovingKeys.","key":"2","section":"guidance"}
M design "Real elements: <button type=button> for actions, <a> for navigation, <label> around inputs. Choice groups use role=radiogroup + aria-checked (Segmented); menus/lists use role=menuitem/option with useRovingKeys." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Dialogs: role=dialog + aria-label, Escape closes, focus moves inside and returns to the opener (Popover and Sheet do this).","key":"3","section":"guidance"}
M design "Dialogs: role=dialog + aria-label, Escape closes, focus moves inside and returns to the opener (Popover and Sheet do this)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Colour is never the only signal: a dot has a word, an error has an icon and text.","key":"4","section":"guidance"}
M design "Colour is never the only signal: a dot has a word, an error has an icon and text." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Keyboard: Tab reaches every action in reading order; Enter/Space activate; nothing needs hover only.","key":"5","section":"guidance"}
M design "Keyboard: Tab reaches every action in reading order; Enter/Space activate; nothing needs hover only." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Contrast: body text uses --nx-text or --nx-text-2, small labels and counts --nx-muted (4.5:1 or better); --nx-faint fails for small text. Morning is where light tints wash out; check it.","key":"6","section":"guidance"}
M design "Contrast: body text uses --nx-text or --nx-text-2, small labels and counts --nx-muted (4.5:1 or better); --nx-faint fails for small text. Morning is where light tints wash out; check it." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"Live regions: toasts already announce; a status that changes in place uses aria-live=polite.","key":"7","section":"guidance"}
M design "Live regions: toasts already announce; a status that changes in place uses aria-live=polite." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"accessibility","data":"WCAG 2.2 (after Addy Osmani's accessibility skill): targets at least 24x24 px (2.5.8), 36 px icon buttons on phone; focus is never hidden under a sticky header, the dock or a toast (2.4.11), so scroll areas get scroll-padding; every drag (Arrange mode, reordering) has a non-drag way to do the same, buttons or keys (2.5.7).","key":"8","section":"guidance"}
M design "WCAG 2.2 (after Addy Osmani's accessibility skill): targets at least 24x24 px (2.5.8), 36 px icon buttons on phone; focus is never hidden under a sticky header, the dock or a toast (2.4.11), so scroll areas get scroll-padding; every drag (Arrange mode, reordering) has a non-drag way to do the same, buttons or keys (2.5.7)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
L design.check-loop v1 -- Render, look, fix: dev UI, light and dark, phone, console, build, proof
-- @record {"chapter":"check-loop","data":{"effect":"Render desktop 1440x900 and phone 390x844 in the given colour scheme; write screenshots + taste-report.json (gate, findings, contrast, overflow, unnamed controls)","pre":"Page served (vite dev URL or file://); waitFor names a selector that exists only once content rendered","returns":{"$cl_type":"t20"},"reversible":true,"schema":"preview.taste","tool":"preview.taste"},"key":"taste","section":"actions"}
A preview.taste(url:str goal?:str#..600 viewports?:[json:"{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"desktop\",\"phone\"]}"] colorScheme?:json:"{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"dark\",\"light\"]}" waitFor?:str delayMs?:0..10000 includeImageData?:json:"{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Inline capped screenshots for the installed desktop Preview, which has no HTTP artifact route.\"}" journey?:json:"{\"type\":\"object\",\"description\":\"Controls to exercise through Laya: actions [{kind: click|fill|select|press, label, value?, expect?}], expect [{kind: selector_text|text_present|selector_exists|url_contains, ...}].\"}" outputDir?:json:"{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional report directory inside the active workspace. Omit to use the managed artifact directory.\"}") -> {gate:str score?:int report:str screenshots:json:"{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"desktop\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}}}" ..} ! -- Render desktop 1440x900 and phone 390x844 in the given colour scheme; write screenshots + taste-report.json (gate, findings, contrast, overflow, unnamed controls)
C preview.taste light-rendered:matches(workspace.read(path:result.report) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"\"gate\": \"blocked\""}} {not:{pattern:"\"measured\": 0,"}}] type:"string"})
C preview.taste dark-rendered:matches(workspace.read(path:result.report) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"\"gate\": \"blocked\""}} {not:{pattern:"\"measured\": 0,"}}] type:"string"})
-- @record {"chapter":"check-loop","data":{"effect":"Return text and full-byte SHA-256; nothing changes","pre":"Text file under the selected workspace (the Neyvia checkout for token files); maxChars bounds the read","returns":{"$cl_type":"t18"},"reversible":true,"schema":"workspace.read","tool":"workspace.read"},"key":"read","section":"actions"}
A workspace.read(path:str maxChars?:1..100000 offset?:0.. startLine?:1.. endLine?:1.. expectedSha256?:str ~"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$") -> {content:str sha256:str ..} -- Return text and full-byte SHA-256; nothing changes
C workspace.read component-css:matches(workspace.read(path:cssPath) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,8}\\b|\\b(rgba?|hsla?)\\("}} {not:{pattern:"transition:\\s*all|\\b[0-9]*\\.?[0-9]+m?s\\b"}} {not:{pattern:"(^|[^-])width:\\s*([4-9][0-9]{2}|[0-9]{4,})px|min-width:\\s*([4-9][0-9]{2}|[0-9]{4,})px|overflow-x:\\s*scroll"}} {not:{pattern:"outline:\\s*(none|0)|:focus(-visible)?\\s*\\{[^}]*box-shadow:\\s*none"}} {pattern:"var\\(--nx-"}] type:"string"})
C workspace.read component-jsx:matches(workspace.read(path:jsxPath) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,8}\\b|\\b(rgba?|hsla?)\\("}} {not:{pattern:"style=\\{\\{[^}]*(color|background|border|boxShadow)"}} {not:{pattern:"<(div|span|li)\\b[^>]*\\bonClick="}} {not:{pattern:"[a-z]!['\\\"<]"}} {not:{pattern:"(?i)click here"}} {pattern:"\\bnx-"}] type:"string"})
C workspace.read build-passed:workspace.read(path:".agent_control/build-check.log") .content has "built in"
C workspace.read build-entrypoint:workspace.read(path:".agent_control/build-check/index.html") .content has "<html"
