-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":{"args":{"path":"docs/design/details-library.md"},"expect":{"op":"schema","path":"content","schema":{"allOf":[{"pattern":"https://rareui\\.com"},{"pattern":"MIT \\+ Commons Clause"},{"pattern":"barvian/number-flow"},{"pattern":"ibelick/motion-primitives"}],"type":"string"}},"tool":"workspace.read"},"key":"details-credited","section":"checks"}
C workspace.read details-credited:matches(workspace.read(path:"docs/design/details-library.md") .content {allOf:[{pattern:"https://rareui\\.com"} {pattern:"MIT \\+ Commons Clause"} {pattern:"barvian/number-flow"} {pattern:"ibelick/motion-primitives"}] type:"string"})
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":{"constraints":"none is the default (Emil's frequency gate: 100+/day or keyboard moments get no motion). rolling-number = a count that changes while you look (done steps, tasks); not for prices or IDs. meter = a fraction you can trust: real value/max, or an estimate that stays under 90 % until done; never a fake percentage. confirm-in-place = an action that cannot be undone and has no Undo toast; recoverable actions (Recycle Bin, archive with Undo) do not ask. strike = a finished item that stays visible. copy = any copy control (it must say Copied or Copy failed). empty-state = nothing to show: say what is missing and one way forward. calm-loading = any loading state that can finish in under a quarter second.","options":["none","rolling-number","meter","confirm-in-place","strike","copy","empty-state","calm-loading"],"question":"Which detail does this moment need?"},"key":"detail-fit","section":"judge"}
J detail-fit none|rolling-number|meter|confirm-in-place|strike|copy|empty-state|calm-loading:"Which detail does this moment need?" -- none is the default (Emil's frequency gate: 100+/day or keyboard moments get no motion). rolling-number = a count that changes while you look (done steps, tasks); not for prices or IDs. meter = a fraction you can trust: real value/max, or an estimate that stays under 90 % until done; never a fake percentage. confirm-in-place = an action that cannot be undone and has no Undo toast; recoverable actions (Recycle Bin, archive with Undo) do not ask. strike = a finished item that stays visible. copy = any copy control (it must say Copied or Copy failed). empty-state = nothing to show: say what is missing and one way forward. calm-loading = any loading state that can finish in under a quarter second.
V J detail-fit -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":{"failure":"A rolling number's faces show up in the page text (an agent or a test reads '0123456789…')","recovery":"Faces are CSS-generated (::before content); keep the visually hidden full number as the only DOM text"},"key":"0","section":"pitfalls"}
X A rolling number's faces show up in the page text (an agent or a test reads '0123456789…') -> Faces are CSS-generated (::before content); keep the visually hidden full number as the only DOM text
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":{"failure":"A column jumps instead of rolling, or rolls nine faces the wrong way","recovery":"Never re-insert a rolling column into the page (it loses its transition); move only nodes whose place changed; direction comes from the value's change (wheelTarget)"},"key":"1","section":"pitfalls"}
X A column jumps instead of rolling, or rolls nine faces the wrong way -> Never re-insert a rolling column into the page (it loses its transition); move only nodes whose place changed; direction comes from the value's change (wheelTarget)
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":{"failure":"A progress bar reaches 100 % while the work still runs","recovery":"Use Meter with startedAt/estimateMs (creep stays under 90 %) and set done only from the real result"},"key":"2","section":"pitfalls"}
X A progress bar reaches 100 % while the work still runs -> Use Meter with startedAt/estimateMs (creep stays under 90 %) and set done only from the real result
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":{"failure":"A confirm dialog for an action that has Undo","recovery":"Do it and offer Undo (the Tidy toast pattern); ConfirmInPlace is only for the irreversible"},"key":"3","section":"pitfalls"}
X A confirm dialog for an action that has Undo -> Do it and offer Undo (the Tidy toast pattern); ConfirmInPlace is only for the irreversible
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":{"failure":"The skeleton flashes for 100 ms on every fast load","recovery":"Gate it with useCalmLoading (240 ms delay, 480 ms minimum)"},"key":"4","section":"pitfalls"}
X The skeleton flashes for 100 ms on every fast load -> Gate it with useCalmLoading (240 ms delay, 480 ms minimum)
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":{"failure":"A silent copy button","recovery":"CopyButton or useCopy: drawn check plus 'Copied', and 'Copy failed' when the clipboard refuses"},"key":"5","section":"pitfalls"}
X A silent copy button -> CopyButton or useCopy: drawn check plus 'Copied', and 'Copy failed' when the clipboard refuses
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":"design-craft's disclosure-state check flags ConfirmInPlace (setOpen without aria-expanded): the trigger is replaced by the question, not expanded, so aria-expanded would always read false. Narrowing candidate (CL-Skill section 7), left as a warn on record.","key":"0","section":"frontier"}
F design-craft's disclosure-state check flags ConfirmInPlace (setOpen without aria-expanded): the trigger is replaced by the question, not expanded, so aria-expanded would always read false. Narrowing candidate (CL-Skill section 7), left as a warn on record.
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":"The kit is web/PWA only. Expo/React Native and the desktop template need their own versions (Reanimated for the wheel, Haptics.selectionAsync for haptic).","key":"1","section":"frontier"}
F The kit is web/PWA only. Expo/React Native and the desktop template need their own versions (Reanimated for the wheel, Haptics.selectionAsync for haptic).
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":"NxFilesApp's copy path uses CopyButton but was not driven live (the Files app needs a signed-in backend; dev fixtures do not cover it); the same component is driven in the chat and the lab.","key":"2","section":"frontier"}
F NxFilesApp's copy path uses CopyButton but was not driven live (the Files app needs a signed-in backend; dev fixtures do not cover it); the same component is driven in the chat and the lab.
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":"Rare UI's licence (MIT + Commons Clause + attribution) forbids redistributing its components; Neyvia's details are original code that takes ideas only, and credit Rare UI visibly anyway. If Paul reads the clause as covering ideas, set template:false on the four rare-ui entries in details.manifest.json.","key":"3","section":"frontier"}
F Rare UI's licence (MIT + Commons Clause + attribution) forbids redistributing its components; Neyvia's details are original code that takes ideas only, and credit Rare UI visibly anyway. If Paul reads the clause as covering ideas, set template:false on the four rare-ui entries in details.manifest.json.
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":"Import from ./details/nxDetails.jsx (one CSS file comes with it). Generated web apps get the same details from details/details.js through the App SDK template (details.manifest.json 'kit').","key":"0","section":"guidance"}
M design "Import from ./details/nxDetails.jsx (one CSS file comes with it). Generated web apps get the same details from details/details.js through the App SDK template (details.manifest.json 'kit')." src:"authored manual" state:verified
