-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":"PRESS ('nx-press' class) on Button/IconButton/CopyButton: scale(0.97) on press with the snappy spring. haptic('tick'|'confirm'): 8 ms vibration on touch phones only, never with reduced motion. Keyboard focus is never animated.","key":"8","section":"guidance"}
M design "PRESS ('nx-press' class) on Button/IconButton/CopyButton: scale(0.97) on press with the snappy spring. haptic('tick'|'confirm'): 8 ms vibration on touch phones only, never with reduced motion. Keyboard focus is never animated." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"details","data":"Sources: Rare UI (Swami Malode, MIT + Commons Clause + attribution, rareui.com: animated-counter, delete-button, task-list, grid-reveal ideas), NumberFlow (Maxwell Barvian, MIT: mask and digit technique), motion-primitives (ibelick, MIT: studied, text-shimmer rejected as a new loop), Sonner and Emil Kowalski's skills (MIT: press scale, exit faster than enter). All Neyvia code is original; docs/design/details-library.md has the full notes.","key":"9","section":"guidance"}
M design "Sources: Rare UI (Swami Malode, MIT + Commons Clause + attribution, rareui.com: animated-counter, delete-button, task-list, grid-reveal ideas), NumberFlow (Maxwell Barvian, MIT: mask and digit technique), motion-primitives (ibelick, MIT: studied, text-shimmer rejected as a new loop), Sonner and Emil Kowalski's skills (MIT: press scale, exit faster than enter). All Neyvia code is original; docs/design/details-library.md has the full notes." src:"authored manual" state:verified
L design.direction v1 -- Visual direction: cool deep backgrounds, rare warm accents, the tree and sun
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":{"effect":"Return an image board of references with facets; nothing is copied","pre":"Query names the surface and job (e.g. 'agent run list dark desktop'); network available","returns":{"$cl_type":"t31"},"reversible":true,"schema":"ui.inspiration.search","tool":"ui.inspiration.search"},"key":"inspiration","section":"actions"}
A ui.inspiration.search(query:str surface?:str platform?:str style?:str color?:str layout?:str limit?:1..24) -> {results:json:"{\"type\":\"array\"}" ..} -- Return an image board of references with facets; nothing is copied
F verify-inspiration "No authored observer check is bound to ui.inspiration.search" -> ask operator blocks:ui.inspiration.search
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":{"goal":"Look at strong references for a surface and keep only principles that fit Neyvia","inputs":{"$cl_type":"t32"},"steps":[{"action":"inspiration","args":{"limit":12,"query":{"$input":"query"}},"save":"board"},{"judge":"reference-transfer"}]},"key":"find-references","section":"procedures"}
P find-references(query:str):board=ui.inspiration.search(limit:12 query:query); J reference-transfer -- Look at strong references for a surface and keep only principles that fit Neyvia
V P find-references -> script why:"typed manual runner; stops at every judgement"
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":{"constraints":"Prefer shipped tools used daily over concept shots. Write the principle and where it would fail; translate it into Neyvia tokens and primitives. Never copy a surface, palette or logo.","options":["adopt-principle","reject"],"question":"Does a reference carry a principle that solves a real problem here?"},"key":"reference-transfer","section":"judge"}
J reference-transfer adopt-principle|reject:"Does a reference carry a principle that solves a real problem here?" -- Prefer shipped tools used daily over concept shots. Write the principle and where it would fail; translate it into Neyvia tokens and primitives. Never copy a surface, palette or logo.
V J reference-transfer -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":{"failure":"Brown or muddy darks","recovery":"Cool the hue toward green/teal/violet and deepen it"},"key":"0","section":"pitfalls"}
X Brown or muddy darks -> Cool the hue toward green/teal/violet and deepen it
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":{"failure":"Orange everywhere to feel warm","recovery":"Warmth is the sun: one hero action and states only"},"key":"1","section":"pitfalls"}
X Orange everywhere to feel warm -> Warmth is the sun: one hero action and states only
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":{"failure":"Dribbble-style glass, giant type, fake charts","recovery":"Real product state, compact type, honest empty states"},"key":"2","section":"pitfalls"}
X Dribbble-style glass, giant type, fake charts -> Real product state, compact type, honest empty states
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":{"failure":"Every block gets an eyebrow label, a numbered marker or an icon tile","recovery":"Run the removal test; keep it only if it carries information"},"key":"3","section":"pitfalls"}
X Every block gets an eyebrow label, a numbered marker or an icon tile -> Run the removal test; keep it only if it carries information
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Paul's verdict on a new look only comes from him seeing it; show screenshots and ask before spreading a new pattern","key":"0","section":"frontier"}
F Paul's verdict on a new look only comes from him seeing it; show screenshots and ask before spreading a new pattern
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Cool, deep backgrounds: Forest near-black green, Sunset twilight violet, Night Green dark water teal; Morning is warm paper with deep leaf greens. Warm colour is rare and means something.","key":"0","section":"guidance"}
M design "Cool, deep backgrounds: Forest near-black green, Sunset twilight violet, Night Green dark water teal; Morning is warm paper with deep leaf greens. Warm colour is rare and means something." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"The sun means something is happening (amber running, gold needs you, the sun gradient for the one hero action). The calm working surface and its actions are green.","key":"1","section":"guidance"}
M design "The sun means something is happening (amber running, gold needs you, the sun gradient for the one hero action). The calm working surface and its actions are green." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Identity: the warm sun-and-tree mark (scripts/brand/neyvia_sun_mark.py) and the growing tree for work. The logo is warm; the UI stays green. Don't recolour the UI to match the logo.","key":"2","section":"guidance"}
M design "Identity: the warm sun-and-tree mark (scripts/brand/neyvia_sun_mark.py) and the growing tree for work. The logo is warm; the UI stays green. Don't recolour the UI to match the logo." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Paul's taste so far: likes Morning; rejected the first muddy dark theme and a brown/maroon Sunset. No brown or maroon surfaces; keep darks cool and deep.","key":"3","section":"guidance"}
M design "Paul's taste so far: likes Morning; rejected the first muddy dark theme and a brown/maroon Sunset. No brown or maroon surfaces; keep darks cool and deep." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Calm first: few boxes, tonal fills over borders, one accent per area, detail on demand. If removing 20-40% of borders, pills and helper lines loses nothing, remove them.","key":"4","section":"guidance"}
M design "Calm first: few boxes, tonal fills over borders, one accent per area, detail on demand. If removing 20-40% of borders, pills and helper lines loses nothing, remove them." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Hierarchy must survive greyscale: size, weight and spacing carry it; colour carries meaning only.","key":"5","section":"guidance"}
M design "Hierarchy must survive greyscale: size, weight and spacing carry it; colour carries meaning only." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Newsreader display type only for a title that greets (Accounts 'You', the new-chat title); the rest is Geist.","key":"6","section":"guidance"}
M design "Newsreader display type only for a title that greets (Accounts 'You', the new-chat title); the rest is Geist." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Blur/glass only where something real shows through (Sunset and Night Green widgets); never decorative.","key":"7","section":"guidance"}
M design "Blur/glass only where something real shows through (Sunset and Night Green widgets); never decorative." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Familiar grammar for typing, menus, files, back/close; spend novelty where Neyvia differs (agents at work, live checklists, movable dashboard).","key":"8","section":"guidance"}
M design "Familiar grammar for typing, menus, files, back/close; spend novelty where Neyvia differs (agents at work, live checklists, movable dashboard)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Layout feel: like Xiaomi HyperOS, every surface is movable and the rest reflows; design components that work in more than one place.","key":"9","section":"guidance"}
M design "Layout feel: like Xiaomi HyperOS, every surface is movable and the rest reflows; design components that work in more than one place." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Spend boldness in one place: one element per screen carries the emphasis (the sun action or a status); everything around it stays quiet. Structure is information: numbers only for real sequences, a label only when the content does not already say it (after Anthropic's frontend-design).","key":"10","section":"guidance"}
M design "Spend boldness in one place: one element per screen carries the emphasis (the sun action or a status); everything around it stays quiet. Structure is information: numbers only for real sequences, a label only when the content does not already say it (after Anthropic's frontend-design)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Two generated-default looks sit close to Neyvia on purpose: warm paper with a serif display (Morning with Newsreader) and near-black with a green accent (Forest). Keep them chosen, not default: Newsreader only for greeting titles, green deep and calm (never acid), no terracotta or brass accents, no tracked uppercase eyebrows.","key":"11","section":"guidance"}
M design "Two generated-default looks sit close to Neyvia on purpose: warm paper with a serif display (Morning with Newsreader) and near-black with a green accent (Forest). Keep them chosen, not default: Newsreader only for greeting titles, green deep and calm (never acid), no terracotta or brass accents, no tracked uppercase eyebrows." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"direction","data":"Removal test before shipping (after Meng To's audit-ai-design-slop): for each border, pill, label, icon and helper line, say what information, state or action it carries; if removing it loses nothing, remove it.","key":"12","section":"guidance"}
M design "Removal test before shipping (after Meng To's audit-ai-design-slop): for each border, pill, label, icon and helper line, say what information, state or action it carries; if removing it loses nothing, remove it." src:"authored manual" state:verified
L design.layout v1 -- Gutters, phone width, no sideways scroll, movable surfaces
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":{"effect":"Return text and full-byte SHA-256; nothing changes","pre":"Text file under the selected workspace (the Neyvia checkout for token files); maxChars bounds the read","returns":{"$cl_type":"t18"},"reversible":true,"schema":"workspace.read","tool":"workspace.read"},"key":"read","section":"actions"}
A workspace.read(path:str maxChars?:1..100000 offset?:0.. startLine?:1.. endLine?:1.. expectedSha256?:str ~"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$") -> {content:str sha256:str ..} -- Return text and full-byte SHA-256; nothing changes
C workspace.read layout-css:matches(workspace.read(path:cssPath) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"(^|[^-])width:\\s*([4-9][0-9]{2}|[0-9]{4,})px|min-width:\\s*([4-9][0-9]{2}|[0-9]{4,})px|overflow-x:\\s*scroll"}}] type:"string"})
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":{"effect":"Render desktop 1440x900 and phone 390x844 in the given colour scheme; write screenshots + taste-report.json (gate, findings, contrast, overflow, unnamed controls)","pre":"Page served (vite dev URL or file://); waitFor names a selector that exists only once content rendered","returns":{"$cl_type":"t20"},"reversible":true,"schema":"preview.taste","tool":"preview.taste"},"key":"taste","section":"actions"}
A preview.taste(url:str goal?:str#..600 viewports?:[json:"{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"desktop\",\"phone\"]}"] colorScheme?:json:"{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"dark\",\"light\"]}" waitFor?:str delayMs?:0..10000 includeImageData?:json:"{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Inline capped screenshots for the installed desktop Preview, which has no HTTP artifact route.\"}" journey?:json:"{\"type\":\"object\",\"description\":\"Controls to exercise through Laya: actions [{kind: click|fill|select|press, label, value?, expect?}], expect [{kind: selector_text|text_present|selector_exists|url_contains, ...}].\"}" outputDir?:json:"{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional report directory inside the active workspace. Omit to use the managed artifact directory.\"}") -> {gate:str score?:int report:str screenshots:json:"{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"desktop\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}}}" ..} ! -- Render desktop 1440x900 and phone 390x844 in the given colour scheme; write screenshots + taste-report.json (gate, findings, contrast, overflow, unnamed controls)
C preview.taste phone-rendered:matches(workspace.read(path:result.report) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"\"gate\": \"blocked\""}} {not:{pattern:"\"measured\": 0,"}}] type:"string"})
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":{"args":{"path":{"$input":"cssPath"}},"expect":{"op":"schema","path":"content","schema":{"allOf":[{"not":{"pattern":"(^|[^-])width:\\s*([4-9][0-9]{2}|[0-9]{4,})px|min-width:\\s*([4-9][0-9]{2}|[0-9]{4,})px|overflow-x:\\s*scroll"}}],"type":"string"}},"tool":"workspace.read"},"key":"layout-css","section":"checks"}
C workspace.read layout-css:matches(workspace.read(path:cssPath) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"(^|[^-])width:\\s*([4-9][0-9]{2}|[0-9]{4,})px|min-width:\\s*([4-9][0-9]{2}|[0-9]{4,})px|overflow-x:\\s*scroll"}}] type:"string"})
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":{"args":{"path":{"$result":"phone.report"}},"expect":{"op":"schema","path":"content","schema":{"allOf":[{"not":{"pattern":"\"gate\": \"blocked\""}},{"not":{"pattern":"\"measured\": 0,"}}],"type":"string"}},"tool":"workspace.read"},"key":"phone-rendered","section":"checks"}
C workspace.read phone-rendered:matches(workspace.read(path:phone.report) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"\"gate\": \"blocked\""}} {not:{pattern:"\"measured\": 0,"}}] type:"string"})
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":{"goal":"Verify a screen's CSS has no wide fixed widths, render it at phone width and decide if it fits","inputs":{"$cl_type":"t33"},"steps":[{"action":"read","args":{"path":{"$input":"cssPath"}},"check":"layout-css","save":"css"},{"action":"taste","args":{"colorScheme":"light","url":{"$input":"url"},"viewports":["phone"],"waitFor":{"$input":"waitFor"}},"check":"phone-rendered","save":"phone"},{"judge":"phone-fit"}]},"key":"phone-check","section":"procedures"}
P phone-check(cssPath:str url:str waitFor:str):css=workspace.read(path:cssPath) C layout-css; phone=preview.taste(colorScheme:"light" url:url viewports:["phone"] waitFor:waitFor) C phone-rendered; J phone-fit -- Verify a screen's CSS has no wide fixed widths, render it at phone width and decide if it fits
V P phone-check -> script why:"typed manual runner; stops at every judgement"
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":{"constraints":"Open the PNG and look: no sideways scroll, no clipped or colliding text, primary action reachable without hunting, nothing under 11px. horizontalOverflowPx > 0 in the report is always rework.","options":["fits","rework"],"question":"Does the phone screenshot read well at 390px?"},"key":"phone-fit","section":"judge"}
J phone-fit fits|rework:"Does the phone screenshot read well at 390px?" -- Open the PNG and look: no sideways scroll, no clipped or colliding text, primary action reachable without hunting, nothing under 11px. horizontalOverflowPx > 0 in the report is always rework.
V J phone-fit -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":{"constraints":"Open docs/evidence/placement-shots/index.html and look at every row: each window fills its place with its title bar and placement buttons, nothing clipped or colliding, narrow places use the app's compact layout, the shell under a full-screen window is hidden.","options":["fits","rework"],"question":"Does every app read well in every placement?"},"key":"placement-look","section":"judge"}
J placement-look fits|rework:"Does every app read well in every placement?" -- Open docs/evidence/placement-shots/index.html and look at every row: each window fills its place with its title bar and placement buttons, nothing clipped or colliding, narrow places use the app's compact layout, the shell under a full-screen window is hidden.
V J placement-look -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":{"constraints":"Open docs/evidence/appdesign/after/sheet-a.png and sheet-b.png (and the final/ pairs). Each app must read as itself in all four themes: terminal ink, PDF paper on a desk, warm notes, graphite 3D, neutral image studio, App Factory showing the app in a frame. Nothing inside an app is painted the theme's green; no text vanishes in Morning; side panel and bubble use the compact layouts. Obscura paints no iframes, WebGL or web fonts: those are judged in a real browser.","options":["fits","rework"],"question":"Does every app look like itself, and beautiful, in every theme?"},"key":"app-identity","section":"judge"}
J app-identity fits|rework:"Does every app look like itself, and beautiful, in every theme?" -- Open docs/evidence/appdesign/after/sheet-a.png and sheet-b.png (and the final/ pairs). Each app must read as itself in all four themes: terminal ink, PDF paper on a desk, warm notes, graphite 3D, neutral image studio, App Factory showing the app in a frame. Nothing inside an app is painted the theme's green; no text vanishes in Morning; side panel and bubble use the compact layouts. Obscura paints no iframes, WebGL or web fonts: those are judged in a real browser.
V J app-identity -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
