-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":"Apps and panes are windows (nxPlacementModel.js, NxPlacement.jsx): open them with os.openApp / os.showPane and never render a stage app inside a region yourself. One layer draws every window over its slot, so a move never remounts the app or reloads its iframes.","key":"9","section":"guidance"}
M design "Apps and panes are windows (nxPlacementModel.js, NxPlacement.jsx): open them with os.openApp / os.showPane and never render a stage app inside a region yourself. One layer draws every window over its slot, so a move never remounts the app or reloads its iframes." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":"Every window offers the same four places with the same controls: title-bar buttons, title-bar drag to drop zones, Alt+Shift+arrows (Home = beside the chat), Esc out of full screen, bubble keys Enter/R/Delete/arrows.","key":"10","section":"guidance"}
M design "Every window offers the same four places with the same controls: title-bar buttons, title-bar drag to drop zones, Alt+Shift+arrows (Home = beside the chat), Esc out of full screen, bubble keys Enter/R/Delete/arrows." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":"A narrow window (side panel, bubble peek, under 640px) is not a phone: read useSurfaceSize().compact (nxSurfaceSize.js) or .nx-surface[data-compact] for a compact layout, not only the viewport media query.","key":"11","section":"guidance"}
