-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":"App Factory, App preview and CiteCraft read their own window, not the screen: App Factory switches to one column (the app first, Brief and Build behind tabs) under 760px of window; native studios stack through @container nxstudio; the App preview canvas shrinks its frame. useSurfaceSize().compact is there for apps that need it in JavaScript.","key":"12","section":"guidance"}
M design "App Factory, App preview and CiteCraft read their own window, not the screen: App Factory switches to one column (the app first, Brief and Build behind tabs) under 760px of window; native studios stack through @container nxstudio; the App preview canvas shrinks its frame. useSurfaceSize().compact is there for apps that need it in JavaScript." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"layout","data":"An app that makes things shows the thing (Paul: 'the App Factory doesn't show the thing being made'): App Factory and App preview draw the app in a frame that fits its target (TargetFrame: a window for native desktop, a browser for a Neyvia local app, an iPhone or Android phone), with a badge saying what it is (Sample, Sketch of your brief, Building, Live) and the build rail flowing under it.","key":"13","section":"guidance"}
M design "An app that makes things shows the thing (Paul: 'the App Factory doesn't show the thing being made'): App Factory and App preview draw the app in a frame that fits its target (TargetFrame: a window for native desktop, a browser for a Neyvia local app, an iPhone or Android phone), with a badge saying what it is (Sample, Sketch of your brief, Building, Live) and the build rail flowing under it." src:"authored manual" state:verified
