-- @record {"chapter":"learned-capabilities","data":"These same native tools are available to agents, App Factory and the taste loop. They never publish or execute generated code.","key":"0","section":"guidance"}
M design "These same native tools are available to agents, App Factory and the taste loop. They never publish or execute generated code." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"learned-capabilities","data":"LAYA Instant: efficiency.laya_learn writes domain/input/label/source with layer personal and user paul for taste; efficiency.laya_query reads it, efficiency.laya_forget removes a source. Service callers use triage(task=manual-routing) with manual ID options, or verify(question=tool_outcome) with a toolId/result receipt and success/failure candidate, under the same selected workspace root. Explicit replay is not a statistical guarantee. Novel inputs use store leave-one-out scores, an out-of-fold agreement filter and a singleton cross-conformal set at nominal 0.95. Scores update on each write. This is empirical admission, not a selective accuracy guarantee; independently held-out families must measure at least 0.95 selective accuracy. Evaluation holdouts never enter neighbours, calibration or exact replay. Duplicate vectors do not multiply support. Image cold encoding is measured separately from warm text writes. Never convert author guesses into quality labels.","key":"1","section":"guidance"}
M design "LAYA Instant: efficiency.laya_learn writes domain/input/label/source with layer personal and user paul for taste; efficiency.laya_query reads it, efficiency.laya_forget removes a source. Service callers use triage(task=manual-routing) with manual ID options, or verify(question=tool_outcome) with a toolId/result receipt and success/failure candidate, under the same selected workspace root. Explicit replay is not a statistical guarantee. Novel inputs use store leave-one-out scores, an out-of-fold agreement filter and a singleton cross-conformal set at nominal 0.95. Scores update on each write. This is empirical admission, not a selective accuracy guarantee; independently held-out families must measure at least 0.95 selective accuracy. Evaluation holdouts never enter neighbours, calibration or exact replay. Duplicate vectors do not multiply support. Image cold encoding is measured separately from warm text writes. Never convert author guesses into quality labels." src:"authored manual" state:verified
L design.motion v1 -- Motion budget, springs, pulses and reduced motion
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":{"effect":"Return text and full-byte SHA-256; nothing changes","pre":"Text file under the selected workspace (the Neyvia checkout for token files); maxChars bounds the read","returns":{"$cl_type":"t18"},"reversible":true,"schema":"workspace.read","tool":"workspace.read"},"key":"read","section":"actions"}
A workspace.read(path:str maxChars?:1..100000 offset?:0.. startLine?:1.. endLine?:1.. expectedSha256?:str ~"^[a-fA-F0-9]{64}$") -> {content:str sha256:str ..} -- Return text and full-byte SHA-256; nothing changes
C workspace.read motion-css:matches(workspace.read(path:cssPath) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"transition:\\s*all|\\b[0-9]*\\.?[0-9]+m?s\\b"}} {not:{pattern:"scale\\(\\s*0(\\.0+)?\\s*\\)"}} {not:{pattern:"\\bease-in\\b(?!-out)"}} {not:{pattern:"(animation|transition)-delay"}} {not:{pattern:"transition(-property)?\\s*:[^;]*\\b(width|height|max-height|margin|padding|top|left)\\b"}}] type:"string"})
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":{"args":{"path":{"$input":"cssPath"}},"expect":{"op":"schema","path":"content","schema":{"allOf":[{"not":{"pattern":"transition:\\s*all|\\b[0-9]*\\.?[0-9]+m?s\\b"}},{"not":{"pattern":"scale\\(\\s*0(\\.0+)?\\s*\\)"}},{"not":{"pattern":"\\bease-in\\b(?!-out)"}},{"not":{"pattern":"(animation|transition)-delay"}},{"not":{"pattern":"transition(-property)?\\s*:[^;]*\\b(width|height|max-height|margin|padding|top|left)\\b"}}],"type":"string"}},"tool":"workspace.read"},"key":"motion-css","section":"checks"}
C workspace.read motion-css:matches(workspace.read(path:cssPath) .content {allOf:[{not:{pattern:"transition:\\s*all|\\b[0-9]*\\.?[0-9]+m?s\\b"}} {not:{pattern:"scale\\(\\s*0(\\.0+)?\\s*\\)"}} {not:{pattern:"\\bease-in\\b(?!-out)"}} {not:{pattern:"(animation|transition)-delay"}} {not:{pattern:"transition(-property)?\\s*:[^;]*\\b(width|height|max-height|margin|padding|top|left)\\b"}}] type:"string"})
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":{"goal":"Confirm the motion tokens, choose the motion a change needs, then verify the CSS stays inside the budget","inputs":{"$cl_type":"t34"},"steps":[{"action":"read","args":{"path":"web/src/neyvia/next/nxTokens.css"},"save":"tokens"},{"judge":"motion-need"},{"action":"read","args":{"path":{"$input":"cssPath"}},"check":"motion-css","save":"css"}]},"key":"check-motion","section":"procedures"}
P check-motion(cssPath:str):tokens=workspace.read(path:"web/src/neyvia/next/nxTokens.css"); J motion-need; css=workspace.read(path:cssPath) C motion-css -- Confirm the motion tokens, choose the motion a change needs, then verify the CSS stays inside the budget
V P check-motion -> script why:"typed manual runner; stops at every judgement"
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":{"constraints":"none is the default; keyboard-initiated or 100+/day actions are always none. feedback = colour/shadow on --nx-fast or --nx-snappy; entrance = existing keyframes (nx-pop-in, nx-stage-in, nx-fade) on --nx-med/--nx-settle, from the trigger for popovers; live-state = StatusDot pulse or NxGrowingTree, never a new loop. All one-shot motion stays inside 180-320 ms; exit quicker than enter.","options":["none","feedback","entrance","live-state"],"question":"What motion does this change need?"},"key":"motion-need","section":"judge"}
J motion-need none|feedback|entrance|live-state:"What motion does this change need?" -- none is the default; keyboard-initiated or 100+/day actions are always none. feedback = colour/shadow on --nx-fast or --nx-snappy; entrance = existing keyframes (nx-pop-in, nx-stage-in, nx-fade) on --nx-med/--nx-settle, from the trigger for popovers; live-state = StatusDot pulse or NxGrowingTree, never a new loop. All one-shot motion stays inside 180-320 ms; exit quicker than enter.
V J motion-need -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":{"failure":"A literal 500ms or 0.6s transition feels laggy and escapes retuning","recovery":"Use the duration tokens; the band is 180-320 ms"},"key":"0","section":"pitfalls"}
X A literal 500ms or 0.6s transition feels laggy and escapes retuning -> Use the duration tokens; the band is 180-320 ms
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":{"failure":"Infinite custom keyframes","recovery":"Reuse StatusDot pulse or NxGrowingTree; they already respect reduced motion"},"key":"1","section":"pitfalls"}
X Infinite custom keyframes -> Reuse StatusDot pulse or NxGrowingTree; they already respect reduced motion
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":{"failure":"An entrance from scale(0) or with ease-in looks like it comes from nowhere and feels late","recovery":"Start at opacity 0 + scale(0.985); use var(--nx-ease) or a spring token"},"key":"2","section":"pitfalls"}
X An entrance from scale(0) or with ease-in looks like it comes from nowhere and feels late -> Start at opacity 0 + scale(0.985); use var(--nx-ease) or a spring token
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":{"failure":"Animating height, width, margin or padding (layout) stutters","recovery":"Animate transform and opacity only; for a disclosure show the content without a height animation"},"key":"3","section":"pitfalls"}
X Animating height, width, margin or padding (layout) stutters -> Animate transform and opacity only; for a disclosure show the content without a height animation
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Track t2-motion (in flight on 2 Oct) retunes --nx-fast to 180ms and --nx-drift to 320ms and adds --nx-lift-1..3 / --nx-edge shadows and --nx-state-caution; once merged, cast shadows use the lift tokens and warnings that ask nothing use caution, not gold","key":"0","section":"frontier"}
F Track t2-motion (in flight on 2 Oct) retunes --nx-fast to 180ms and --nx-drift to 320ms and adds --nx-lift-1..3 / --nx-edge shadows and --nx-state-caution; once merged, cast shadows use the lift tokens and warnings that ask nothing use caution, not gold
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Press feedback: Button and IconButton have no :active response yet (only .nx-send scales to 0.95). Emil Kowalski's scale(0.97) on --nx-snappy fits the band; it changes nxShell.css (shared), so it belongs to the motion track.","key":"1","section":"frontier"}
F Press feedback: Button and IconButton have no :active response yet (only .nx-send scales to 0.95). Emil Kowalski's scale(0.97) on --nx-snappy fits the band; it changes nxShell.css (shared), so it belongs to the motion track.
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Interruptible gesture motion (apple-design: respond on press, velocity handoff, momentum projection) for the phone sheet and the docked chat.","key":"2","section":"frontier"}
F Interruptible gesture motion (apple-design: respond on press, velocity handoff, momentum projection) for the phone sheet and the docked chat.
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Budget: every one-shot transition lands between 180 and 320 ms. Durations are tokens only, never literal ms or s: --nx-fast (hover, colour), --nx-med (pop-in, fade), --nx-snappy with --nx-spring-snappy (UI feedback), --nx-settle with --nx-spring-settle (panels, the docked chat), --nx-drift (slow fills, ambient). Read nxTokens.css for today's values.","key":"0","section":"guidance"}
M design "Budget: every one-shot transition lands between 180 and 320 ms. Durations are tokens only, never literal ms or s: --nx-fast (hover, colour), --nx-med (pop-in, fade), --nx-snappy with --nx-spring-snappy (UI feedback), --nx-settle with --nx-spring-settle (panels, the docked chat), --nx-drift (slow fills, ambient). Read nxTokens.css for today's values." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Write transition: <property> var(--nx-fast) var(--nx-ease) or transform var(--nx-snappy) var(--nx-spring-snappy). Name the properties; never transition: all.","key":"1","section":"guidance"}
M design "Write transition: <property> var(--nx-fast) var(--nx-ease) or transform var(--nx-snappy) var(--nx-spring-snappy). Name the properties; never transition: all." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Animate transform and opacity only. Entrances: opacity from 0 plus translateY(4-6px) and scale(0.985) at most (keyframes nx-pop-in, nx-stage-in, nx-fade already exist).","key":"2","section":"guidance"}
M design "Animate transform and opacity only. Entrances: opacity from 0 plus translateY(4-6px) and scale(0.985) at most (keyframes nx-pop-in, nx-stage-in, nx-fade already exist)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Running state = opacity pulse (StatusDot pulse: 1.6 s to 35% opacity) or the growing tree. No bouncing, shaking or spinning icons except Spinner.","key":"3","section":"guidance"}
M design "Running state = opacity pulse (StatusDot pulse: 1.6 s to 35% opacity) or the growing tree. No bouncing, shaking or spinning icons except Spinner." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Reduced motion: nxTokens.css cuts every .nx animation and transition to 1 ms under prefers-reduced-motion. Motion driven from JS must check useMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)'); decorative loops also set animation: none there.","key":"4","section":"guidance"}
M design "Reduced motion: nxTokens.css cuts every .nx animation and transition to 1 ms under prefers-reduced-motion. Motion driven from JS must check useMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)'); decorative loops also set animation: none there." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Nothing moves by itself when idle; motion answers an action or a state change. Lists don't stagger.","key":"5","section":"guidance"}
M design "Nothing moves by itself when idle; motion answers an action or a state change. Lists don't stagger." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Should it move at all (frequency gate, after Emil Kowalski's emil-design-eng): keyboard-initiated actions and anything seen 100+ times a day get no motion; tens a day get colour only; occasional moments (popover, sheet, toast) get the standard entrance; rare ones may get more. When unsure, delete the motion.","key":"6","section":"guidance"}
M design "Should it move at all (frequency gate, after Emil Kowalski's emil-design-eng): keyboard-initiated actions and anything seen 100+ times a day get no motion; tens a day get colour only; occasional moments (popover, sheet, toast) get the standard entrance; rare ones may get more. When unsure, delete the motion." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Nothing appears from nothing: entrances start at opacity 0 with scale(0.985) or translateY(4-6px), never scale(0). Popovers scale from their trigger (transform-origin on the anchor side); modals from the centre. Exit is quicker than enter (exit on --nx-fast, enter on --nx-med or --nx-settle). Never ease-in on UI (review-animations standards 3 and 5).","key":"7","section":"guidance"}
M design "Nothing appears from nothing: entrances start at opacity 0 with scale(0.985) or translateY(4-6px), never scale(0). Popovers scale from their trigger (transform-origin on the anchor side); modals from the centre. Exit is quicker than enter (exit on --nx-fast, enter on --nx-med or --nx-settle). Never ease-in on UI (review-animations standards 3 and 5)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Hover movement (translate, scale) only inside @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine); colour-only hover can stay outside. Rapidly repeated UI (toggles, toasts) uses transitions, which retarget mid-way, not keyframes, which restart.","key":"8","section":"guidance"}
M design "Hover movement (translate, scale) only inside @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine); colour-only hover can stay outside. Rapidly repeated UI (toggles, toasts) uses transitions, which retarget mid-way, not keyframes, which restart." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"The design-craft CL-Skill (craft chapter) checks all of this mechanically: transition-all, literal-duration, scale-zero, ease-in, layout-animated, hover-motion, stagger, loops, js-motion-reduced.","key":"9","section":"guidance"}
M design "The design-craft CL-Skill (craft chapter) checks all of this mechanically: transition-all, literal-duration, scale-zero, ease-in, layout-animated, hover-motion, stagger, loops, js-motion-reduced." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Windows never jump between places (NxPlacement): a move glides left/top/width/height on the settle spring (is-moving), collapsing folds the window toward its bubble's point with a transform and fades it (is-folding), and restoring unfolds it out of the bubble (is-unfolding). While a new slot is being measured the window stays where it was. Opening fades a window in (is-entering) and closing fades it out (is-leaving), so one app replacing another crossfades. All of it is off under reduced motion.","key":"10","section":"guidance"}
M design "Windows never jump between places (NxPlacement): a move glides left/top/width/height on the settle spring (is-moving), collapsing folds the window toward its bubble's point with a transform and fades it (is-folding), and restoring unfolds it out of the bubble (is-unfolding). While a new slot is being measured the window stays where it was. Opening fades a window in (is-entering) and closing fades it out (is-leaving), so one app replacing another crossfades. All of it is off under reduced motion." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"motion","data":"Loading inside a window is a quiet shimmer of text lines (.nx-stage-loading in nxAppSkins.css), never a spinner in the middle of an empty app. A live preview never flashes: LiveApp (NeyviaAppFactoryCanvas.jsx) loads a new address in a second iframe and crossfades only once it has painted.","key":"11","section":"guidance"}
M design "Loading inside a window is a quiet shimmer of text lines (.nx-stage-loading in nxAppSkins.css), never a spinner in the middle of an empty app. A live preview never flashes: LiveApp (NeyviaAppFactoryCanvas.jsx) loads a new address in a second iframe and crossfades only once it has painted." src:"authored manual" state:verified
