P theme-component(cssPath:str jsxPath:str):themes=workspace.read(path:"web/src/neyvia/next/nxThemes.css"); J colour-role; css=workspace.read(path:cssPath) C component-css; jsx=workspace.read(path:jsxPath) C component-jsx -- Give a component Neyvia's colours using only tokens, then verify its CSS and JSX against the colour rules
V P theme-component -> script why:"typed manual runner; stops at every judgement"
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":{"constraints":"calm = surface/line/text tokens only; action = accent family, one filled primary per area; state = the four state tokens with text beside them; hero = --nx-sun, at most one per screen. Pick the quietest role that still says what it must. Choose, write the CSS, then resume.","options":["calm","action","state","hero"],"question":"Which role does each coloured part of the component play?"},"key":"colour-role","section":"judge"}
J colour-role calm|action|state|hero:"Which role does each coloured part of the component play?" -- calm = surface/line/text tokens only; action = accent family, one filled primary per area; state = the four state tokens with text beside them; hero = --nx-sun, at most one per screen. Pick the quietest role that still says what it must. Choose, write the CSS, then resume.
V J colour-role -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":{"failure":"Raw hex/rgba in a component","recovery":"Use the token; if none fits, add a named token to all four theme blocks in nxThemes.css"},"key":"0","section":"pitfalls"}
X Raw hex/rgba in a component -> Use the token; if none fits, add a named token to all four theme blocks in nxThemes.css
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":{"failure":"Small text in --nx-faint (preview.taste blocks it: 2.6-3.2:1 in Morning and Forest)","recovery":"Use --nx-muted at 11px or more; .nx-kbd and .nx-seg-count were fixed this way"},"key":"1","section":"pitfalls"}
X Small text in --nx-faint (preview.taste blocks it: 2.6-3.2:1 in Morning and Forest) -> Use --nx-muted at 11px or more; .nx-kbd and .nx-seg-count were fixed this way
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":{"failure":"Looks right in Forest only","recovery":"Morning flips contrast and Sunset's accent is orange: check light and dark at least, all four when the accent carries meaning"},"key":"2","section":"pitfalls"}
X Looks right in Forest only -> Morning flips contrast and Sunset's accent is orange: check light and dark at least, all four when the accent carries meaning
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":{"failure":"Gold used as decoration","recovery":"Gold means needs you; decorative warmth comes from --nx-ambient/--nx-dapple"},"key":"3","section":"pitfalls"}
X Gold used as decoration -> Gold means needs you; decorative warmth comes from --nx-ambient/--nx-dapple
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":{"failure":"White text on --nx-accent-soft or on Morning surfaces","recovery":"White only on filled --nx-accent; on tints use --nx-accent-text or --nx-text"},"key":"4","section":"pitfalls"}
X White text on --nx-accent-soft or on Morning surfaces -> White only on filled --nx-accent; on tints use --nx-accent-text or --nx-text
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":{"failure":"An app painted with the shell's green (or orange, or sea-green) accent","recovery":"Give the app a skin in nxAppSkinModel.js; inside a window --nx-accent is the app's own"},"key":"5","section":"pitfalls"}
X An app painted with the shell's green (or orange, or sea-green) accent -> Give the app a skin in nxAppSkinModel.js; inside a window --nx-accent is the app's own
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":{"failure":"A literal white or near-black in a classic screen that vanishes in Morning","recovery":"Override it in nxAppSkins.css under [data-nx-skin] with the token, then check the Morning shot"},"key":"6","section":"pitfalls"}
X A literal white or near-black in a classic screen that vanishes in Morning -> Override it in nxAppSkins.css under [data-nx-skin] with the token, then check the Morning shot
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Theme tokens still have no per-theme contrast tool; app skins do (the appskin.skinPalette contract measures every text colour on every surface). Iframe content (generated apps, web pages, the 3D scene) keeps its own colours.","key":"0","section":"frontier"}
F Theme tokens still have no per-theme contrast tool; app skins do (the appskin.skinPalette contract measures every text colour on every surface). Iframe content (generated apps, web pages, the 3D scene) keeps its own colours.
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Theme ids: dark = Forest (default), light = Morning, sunset = Sunset, night = Night Green. Set on the root as data-nx-theme; portals (Popover, Sheet) copy it.","key":"0","section":"guidance"}
M design "Theme ids: dark = Forest (default), light = Morning, sunset = Sunset, night = Night Green. Set on the root as data-nx-theme; portals (Popover, Sheet) copy it." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Surfaces back to front: --nx-bg, --nx-sidebar, --nx-panel, --nx-raised (cards), --nx-raised-2 (selected segment, nested raised). Hover --nx-hover; pressed/selected --nx-active.","key":"1","section":"guidance"}
M design "Surfaces back to front: --nx-bg, --nx-sidebar, --nx-panel, --nx-raised (cards), --nx-raised-2 (selected segment, nested raised). Hover --nx-hover; pressed/selected --nx-active." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Lines: --nx-line (dividers, card ring), --nx-line-strong (outline buttons, inputs). Draw borders as box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--nx-line), not border, so sizes don't shift.","key":"2","section":"guidance"}
M design "Lines: --nx-line (dividers, card ring), --nx-line-strong (outline buttons, inputs). Draw borders as box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--nx-line), not border, so sizes don't shift." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Text: --nx-text (titles, values), --nx-text-2 (body, button labels), --nx-muted (secondary, help, counts, shortcuts). --nx-faint is about 3:1 on its surfaces: only for non-essential meta at 12px or more, never for counts, labels or anything Paul must read.","key":"3","section":"guidance"}
M design "Text: --nx-text (titles, values), --nx-text-2 (body, button labels), --nx-muted (secondary, help, counts, shortcuts). --nx-faint is about 3:1 on its surfaces: only for non-essential meta at 12px or more, never for counts, labels or anything Paul must read." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Actions: --nx-accent (primary fill, white label), --nx-accent-hi (hover, live dot, focused input edge), --nx-accent-text (links, accent words), --nx-accent-soft (selected row tint).","key":"4","section":"guidance"}
M design "Actions: --nx-accent (primary fill, white label), --nx-accent-hi (hover, live dot, focused input edge), --nx-accent-text (links, accent words), --nx-accent-soft (selected row tint)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"States, one meaning each: --nx-state-running (amber: working), --nx-state-needs (gold: needs Paul), --nx-state-ok (green), --nx-state-error (red). Tints: --nx-gold-soft, --nx-green-soft, --nx-red-soft.","key":"5","section":"guidance"}
M design "States, one meaning each: --nx-state-running (amber: working), --nx-state-needs (gold: needs Paul), --nx-state-ok (green), --nx-state-error (red). Tints: --nx-gold-soft, --nx-green-soft, --nx-red-soft." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"--nx-sun (gradient) with --nx-sun-ink text is the single hero action of a screen (e.g. Start). Everything else uses the accent.","key":"6","section":"guidance"}
M design "--nx-sun (gradient) with --nx-sun-ink text is the single hero action of a screen (e.g. Start). Everything else uses the accent." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Depth: card = background var(--nx-raised) + box-shadow var(--nx-card-shadow) + radius 14-16px; popover = var(--nx-shadow-pop); overlay dim = var(--nx-scrim); focus = var(--nx-focus).","key":"7","section":"guidance"}
M design "Depth: card = background var(--nx-raised) + box-shadow var(--nx-card-shadow) + radius 14-16px; popover = var(--nx-shadow-pop); overlay dim = var(--nx-scrim); focus = var(--nx-focus)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Atmosphere: --nx-ambient (low sun + leaf light) and --nx-dapple (sun patches, stars, specks) only on one hero card or an empty canvas: background: var(--nx-ambient), var(--nx-raised).","key":"8","section":"guidance"}
M design "Atmosphere: --nx-ambient (low sun + leaf light) and --nx-dapple (sun patches, stars, specks) only on one hero card or an empty canvas: background: var(--nx-ambient), var(--nx-raised)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Tints come from tokens: color-mix(in srgb, var(--nx-gold) 18%, transparent). No hex, rgb() or hsl() in component CSS.","key":"9","section":"guidance"}
M design "Tints come from tokens: color-mix(in srgb, var(--nx-gold) 18%, transparent). No hex, rgb() or hsl() in component CSS." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Type: --nx-font Geist (UI), --nx-mono Geist Mono (paths, ids, code numbers), --nx-display Newsreader (greeting titles only, weight 500, 19-27px). Sizes --nx-fs-xs 11, -sm 12, --nx-fs 13 (base), -md 14, -prose 14.5, -lg 16, -xl 20.","key":"10","section":"guidance"}
M design "Type: --nx-font Geist (UI), --nx-mono Geist Mono (paths, ids, code numbers), --nx-display Newsreader (greeting titles only, weight 500, 19-27px). Sizes --nx-fs-xs 11, -sm 12, --nx-fs 13 (base), -md 14, -prose 14.5, -lg 16, -xl 20." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Weights: 400 body, 500 labels/buttons, 600 titles and counts. Changing numbers get font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums.","key":"11","section":"guidance"}
M design "Weights: 400 body, 500 labels/buttons, 600 titles and counts. Changing numbers get font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Radii: --nx-r-xs 5, --nx-r-sm 7 (buttons, inputs), --nx-r 10, --nx-r-lg 14 (cards, panels), --nx-r-pill (counts, badges). Inner radius = outer radius minus padding.","key":"12","section":"guidance"}
M design "Radii: --nx-r-xs 5, --nx-r-sm 7 (buttons, inputs), --nx-r 10, --nx-r-lg 14 (cards, panels), --nx-r-pill (counts, badges). Inner radius = outer radius minus padding." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Density: data-nx-density calm|workshop|grove changes only --nx-row-pad, --nx-row-gap, --nx-sidebar-w. List rows use those, never fixed paddings.","key":"13","section":"guidance"}
M design "Density: data-nx-density calm|workshop|grove changes only --nx-row-pad, --nx-row-gap, --nx-sidebar-w. List rows use those, never fixed paddings." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Paul's own theme is changed with neyvia.view.theme; components never read the theme, they only use the tokens.","key":"14","section":"guidance"}
M design "Paul's own theme is changed with neyvia.view.theme; components never read the theme, they only use the tokens." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Elevation is layered and neutral (after Meng To's beautiful-shadows): a 1px ring plus soft layers, one strength per state. Cards use --nx-card-shadow, lifted surfaces --nx-lift-1..3, popovers --nx-shadow-pop; never stack two shadow tokens or put --nx-lift-3 on a dense list. A new recipe goes into nxThemes.css per theme (black shadows vanish on Forest), never as raw rgba in a component.","key":"15","section":"guidance"}
M design "Elevation is layered and neutral (after Meng To's beautiful-shadows): a 1px ring plus soft layers, one strength per state. Cards use --nx-card-shadow, lifted surfaces --nx-lift-1..3, popovers --nx-shadow-pop; never stack two shadow tokens or put --nx-lift-3 on a dense list. A new recipe goes into nxThemes.css per theme (black shadows vanish on Forest), never as raw rgba in a component." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Morning uses canopy light on warm paper #f5f1e6, forest ink #17221a, deep leaf #245a35 and mid leaf #3a774b. One low sun at top-left lights selected rows and cards (#fffdf9/white); green-grey --nx-shade falls down-right. The moss-paper sidebar shades #ebe9da to #dfe5d1; leaf light pools bottom-right. Sun warmth and komorebi appear only during activity. Running text uses ochre #7a4f08; bright amber stays in dots and fills. Check text contrast at 4.5:1 or better. The App SDK template, details kit and Scroll Study share this recipe; source: docs/NEYVIA_BRAND.md, R3 Morning.","key":"16","section":"guidance"}
M design "Morning uses canopy light on warm paper #f5f1e6, forest ink #17221a, deep leaf #245a35 and mid leaf #3a774b. One low sun at top-left lights selected rows and cards (#fffdf9/white); green-grey --nx-shade falls down-right. The moss-paper sidebar shades #ebe9da to #dfe5d1; leaf light pools bottom-right. Sun warmth and komorebi appear only during activity. Running text uses ochre #7a4f08; bright amber stays in dots and fills. Check text contrast at 4.5:1 or better. The App SDK template, details kit and Scroll Study share this recipe; source: docs/NEYVIA_BRAND.md, R3 Morning." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Apps wear skins, not the theme (Paul: 'having the theme green doesn't mean everything must be green'). NxPlacement puts nxAppSkinModel's skinTokens(skin, theme) on each app window as --nx-* values, so components keep using the token names and follow the app's own look: code (Terminal, files, diffs), reader (PDF desk under white paper), notebook (Notes, warm paper and terracotta ink), finder (Files, kind-coloured tiles), web (Browser, App preview), monitor (computer-use preview, LAYA), studio (App Factory, Mobile Studio), graphite (3D), darkroom (Image Studio: neutral grey, paper-white actions, never a loud accent next to photos), scholar (CiteCraft). The shell chrome keeps the theme; inside a window --nx-ambient and --nx-dapple are the app's own quiet light, never the theme's.","key":"17","section":"guidance"}
M design "Apps wear skins, not the theme (Paul: 'having the theme green doesn't mean everything must be green'). NxPlacement puts nxAppSkinModel's skinTokens(skin, theme) on each app window as --nx-* values, so components keep using the token names and follow the app's own look: code (Terminal, files, diffs), reader (PDF desk under white paper), notebook (Notes, warm paper and terracotta ink), finder (Files, kind-coloured tiles), web (Browser, App preview), monitor (computer-use preview, LAYA), studio (App Factory, Mobile Studio), graphite (3D), darkroom (Image Studio: neutral grey, paper-white actions, never a loud accent next to photos), scholar (CiteCraft). The shell chrome keeps the theme; inside a window --nx-ambient and --nx-dapple are the app's own quiet light, never the theme's." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"A skin has a dark and a light base; Forest uses the dark one as is; Morning, Sunset and Night Green shift only the surfaces, toward Morning's warm paper, dusk violet or deep water, by the skin's own tint (the darkroom never shifts). Text and accents never take the theme's hue. New app: add its id to APP_SKIN (or PANE_SKIN) in nxAppSkinModel.js; a new skin needs both bases and passes the appskin contracts (AA text on every surface and hover, no green surface or accent).","key":"18","section":"guidance"}
M design "A skin has a dark and a light base; Forest uses the dark one as is; Morning, Sunset and Night Green shift only the surfaces, toward Morning's warm paper, dusk violet or deep water, by the skin's own tint (the darkroom never shifts). Text and accents never take the theme's hue. New app: add its id to APP_SKIN (or PANE_SKIN) in nxAppSkinModel.js; a new skin needs both bases and passes the appskin contracts (AA text on every surface and hover, no green surface or accent)." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"tokens-themes","data":"Derived tokens resolve where they are declared: nxAppSkins.css re-declares --nx-state-ok, --nx-caution-*, --nx-lift-* and --nx-edge inside [data-nx-skin] so they follow the skin. A classic screen with literal colours gets its overrides there too, scoped by [data-nx-skin].","key":"19","section":"guidance"}
M design "Derived tokens resolve where they are declared: nxAppSkins.css re-declares --nx-state-ok, --nx-caution-*, --nx-lift-* and --nx-edge inside [data-nx-skin] so they follow the skin. A classic screen with literal colours gets its overrides there too, scoped by [data-nx-skin]." src:"authored manual" state:verified
L design.workflow v1 -- Executable design method: chronological mechanism and measured quality
